# Copy this file to `.env` (same folder) and fill in ONE key to enable the AI clinical narrative.
# The app loads `.env` automatically from the project root — no need to `export` in every terminal.
# The narrative is an EXPLANATION layer only; it never changes the model's predictions, so the
# provider is interchangeable. With no key set, the demo still works (deterministic templated report).
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # then edit .env and paste your key
#
# Set ONE of these (preference order Claude > DeepSeek > Gemini):

# DeepSeek — cheap, OpenAI-compatible
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat

# Google Gemini  (free tier at aistudio.google.com/apikey)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest      # a moving alias -> always a current model

# Anthropic Claude
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Force a specific provider even if several keys are set: anthropic | deepseek | gemini
# AMR_LLM_PROVIDER=deepseek
